//! # OSDL Grammar (pest PEG)
//!
//! The OSDL surface syntax is intentionally token-minimal:
//!
//! ```text
//! # comments start with '#'
//! use user                       # module import (unquoted, ::-separated)
//! use billing::invoice
//! User                  # model declaration (top-level, no indentation)
//!   id uuid -pk         # field: name, type, intent flag(s)
//!   email string -uniq
//!   created_at datetime -tz
//!   posts -relation Post          # a relation to another model
//!   author User.id                # an explicit foreign key (Model.field)
//!   profile_id                    # omitted type -> inferred foreign key
//!   bio string -default ""        # default value may be a quoted string
//! ```
//!
//! Indentation is the only structural punctuation: a top-level line (indent 0)
//! begins a `Model`; any indented line adds a `Field` to the most recently
//! declared model. Each source line is terminated by a newline (not `EOI`),
//! which keeps the `line*` repetition strictly progressing.
//!
//! Whitespace handling is explicit: leading indentation is captured by `indent`
//! (so it is NOT swallowed as implicit whitespace), and a single space
//! separates a field name from its type/intent tokens via `sp`.

file    = { SOI ~ line* ~ EOI }

line    = { indent ~ body ~ newline }
// `word` is tried before `name` so that dash-words (e.g. `default-type`,
// `foo-bar`) parse as a single `Word` token instead of `name` greedily
// matching only their alphabetic prefix. Model names are also emitted as
// `Word` tokens and the parser accepts either `Name` or `Word` for a
// top-level model/known-model declaration.
body    = { use_stmt | type_decl | view_line | seed_line | word ~ (sp? ~ token)* | name ~ (sp? ~ token)* | token ~ (sp? ~ token)* | comment_part | doc_comment | "" }

// A seed-data block header: `seed Model`. The rows live on following
// indented continuation lines and are captured verbatim by the parser (like
// view queries), so each row's `column=value` pairs need no grammar shaping.
seed_line = { seed_kw ~ sp ~ ident }
seed_kw   = @{ "seed" }

// A view (read-model) declaration: `view Name (field type, ...) [-materialized] = QUERY`.
// The projection (before `=`) is structured; the QUERY (after `=`) is free-form
// SQL/aggregation text captured verbatim (including `*`, `.`, `(`, `)`), so it
// never needs to satisfy the structured `word`/`reference` tokenizer.
view_line = { view_kw ~ sp ~ view_head ~ sp? ~ equals ~ sp? ~ view_query }
view_kw   = @{ "view" }
// name + optional projection fields + optional `-materialized`, up to the `=`.
// Uses a restricted `view_word` (identifiers only, no `=`) so the separator is
// never swallowed by the projection; commas between projection fields are
// skipped.
view_head = { (sp? ~ (view_flag | view_word | comma))* }
view_word = @{ ident_char+ }
comma     = @{ "," }
view_flag = @{ "-" ~ "materialized" }
// Everything after the first `=` to end-of-line is the query (raw).
view_query = @{ (!newline_char ~ ANY)* }

// A module import: `use path::to::module` (unquoted, `::`-separated). Resolved
// by the project loader into additional source files merged into one AST.
use_stmt    = { use_kw ~ sp ~ module_path }
use_kw      = @{ "use" }
module_path = @{ ident ~ ("::" ~ ident)* }

// A custom type / value object: `type Email = string -check "x ~ 'y'"`.
// Expands inlinely to its base scalar plus inherited intents/check.
type_decl   = { type_kw ~ sp ~ ident ~ sp ~ equals ~ sp ~ type_rhs }
type_kw     = @{ "type" }
equals      = @{ "=" }
type_rhs    = { word ~ (sp ~ token)* }

indent  = @{ (" " | "\t")* }

name    = @{ ident_char+ }
// A dash-word (e.g. `default-type`, `foo-bar`) must parse via `word`, not as a
// `name` prefix. `body` orders the alternatives so a bare `name` is accepted
// for model declarations, while a `name` followed by content requires at
// least one `sp ~ token` — preventing `name` from greedily matching only the
// prefix of a dash-word and then failing at `newline`.
token   = { flag | reference | quoted | word }
sp      = _{ " " }

// Intent flags always begin with '-'.
flag    = @{ "-" ~ (ASCII_ALPHA | "_") ~ (ASCII_ALPHANUMERIC | "_")* }
// A cross-model reference: Model.field (the '.' is the only operator).
reference = @{ ident ~ "." ~ ident }
// A quoted string literal (inner content; the surrounding quotes are stripped).
// Used for values such as `-default ""` or `-default "pending"`.
quoted  = @{ "\"" ~ quoted_inner ~ "\"" }
quoted_inner = @{ (!"\"" ~ (!newline_char ~ ANY))* }
// `word` carries type names, relation targets, `-enum` value lists
// (which may contain commas, e.g. `active,inactive`), `config`-block
// keys/values (which may contain dashes, e.g. `default-type`, and an
// equals sign, e.g. `field=deleted_at`), and view-query separators
// (a lone `=` tokenizes as `Word("=")` so `view V = SELECT ...` parses).
word    = @{ ("," | "=" | ident_char) ~ (ident_char | "," | "-" | "=")* }

ident_char = _{ ASCII_ALPHANUMERIC | "_" }
ident      = @{ ident_char+ }

comment_part = { "#" ~ (!newline_char ~ ANY)* }

// A documentation comment: `/// text`. Attached to the *next* model or field
// declaration (whichever follows, at the matching indent). Multiple consecutive
// `///` lines are accumulated. Not a structural token — purely documentation.
doc_comment = { "///" ~ (!newline_char ~ ANY)* }

newline      = _{ "\r\n" | "\n" | "\r" }
newline_char = _{ "\n" | "\r" }
